From f42d384260fdf9c31d3529be1be37cdb9bcea186 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 20:02:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SCSP integration: the sound 68000's interrupt chain is
 asserted now (SND-01)

The previous revision of this fixture recorded an open finding (the handler
counter never advanced, pc_open=ffffba90).  It was a fixture bug with one
cause: COUNTER and UNMASKED were undeclared Lua globals, and a nil address
argument to a debugger write lands on address 0 instead of raising an error.
ssp:write_u32(COUNTER, 0) therefore zeroed the initial-SSP vector (the CPU
came out of reset with SP=0 and pushed exception frames below address zero),
and read_counter() read address 0, so the handler's real increments were
invisible.  The trap is silent, so the matrix that pinned it down is in the
evidence: write_u32(0x7200,0), write_u32(0x7200,nonzero) and
write_u16(0x7200,0) all leave vector 0 alone, a nil address write does not.

With the fixture fixed the interrupt chain is measured and asserted end to
end on all four profiles (saturnjp interpreter, saturnjp DRC, saturneu DRC,
stvbios DRC; SCSP_INT PASS cases=49): with the mask closed the request is
pending and the count stays 0; once the uploaded program opens the mask the
guest's level 6 autovector handler runs continuously (9 entries at the first
sample, 111 after 300 ms, 215 after the next 300 ms, identical on every
profile), the level 7 counter stays 0 (proving level 6), the supervisor stack
is back at 0007fff0 after 215 exceptions, and the guest's SCIRE clears each
request.  The fixture now declares every value it uses and re-checks the
initial SSP before releasing the reset.

Refreshes the four profiles' logs/reports/invocations, rewrites the evidence
README's finding section as the resolution, updates the SND-01 bullet and the
CI phase expectation (cases=49).

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
